# =============================================================================
# Support Desk — Docker build context exclusions
#
# Keeps the build context small and guarantees that local runtime data and
# secrets never enter an image. `public/` and `prisma/` are deliberately NOT
# excluded — they are required inside the image.
# =============================================================================

# --- Dependencies & build artifacts ---
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
next-env.d.ts

# --- Version control & CI (not needed inside the image) ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Local runtime data (never bake data or secrets into images) ---
db
storage
backups
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Workspace / sandbox artifacts ---
upload
download
tool-results
skills
tests
examples
mini-services
docs
.zscripts
.claude
.z-ai-config

# --- Logs ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Secrets / env files (real .env must never enter the image) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Files that are not needed inside the image ---
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.caddy.yml
Caddyfile
deploy
